00:37:15.570 --> 00:37:18.540
And then, one person asked
about why you shouldn't

00:37:18.540 --> 00:37:21.810
spot weld galvanized steel.

00:37:21.810 --> 00:37:24.060
And when anything is galvanized,
what you're doing is,

00:37:24.060 --> 00:37:28.950
you're coating it with zinc
so that it doesn't rust.

00:37:28.950 --> 00:37:30.660
And when you try
to weld anything

00:37:30.660 --> 00:37:33.870
with zinc coatings on it, you
vaporize the zinc coating,

00:37:33.870 --> 00:37:35.770
and it's pretty toxic to you.

00:37:35.770 --> 00:37:38.790
So if you're doing it in a
really well-ventilated area

00:37:38.790 --> 00:37:40.900
or you're doing it outdoors,
it's not a big deal.

00:37:40.900 --> 00:37:43.200
But if you're doing it
indoors, it's toxic.

00:37:43.200 --> 00:37:45.300
So you want to
make sure you avoid

00:37:45.300 --> 00:37:47.730
welding galvanized materials.

